distribute this software is freely granted, provided that this notice is
preserved"). Only the special-function kernels are vendored; their internal
exp/pow/log/floor calls are routed to Rust std.

This product depends on the `jiff` crate (used only by
crates/crabgresql-types/src/tz.rs for IANA time-zone offset and DST resolution
behind `timestamp with time zone`):

  Copyright (c) 2024 Andrew Gallant (github.com/BurntSushi/jiff)

licensed under Unlicense OR MIT. Jiff bundles a compiled copy of the IANA Time
Zone Database (public domain, github.com/eggert/tz) via the
`tzdb-bundle-always` feature.

The time-zone abbreviation table in crates/crabgresql-types/src/tz.rs (e.g.
`PST` = -08:00, `MSK` -> Europe/Moscow) reproduces values from PostgreSQL's
`src/timezone/tznames/Default` data file — borrowed as data, not source, under
the PostgreSQL License (see the clean-room policy in AGENTS.md).
